SolveSpace constraint test files (test data only)
=================================================

Files:      every *.slvs below this directory
Upstream:   https://github.com/solvespace/solvespace  (path: test/constraint/)
Commit:     5bb74ad2 (master at the time of import, 2026-10-20)
Copyright:  (c) the SolveSpace authors
Licence:    GPL-3.0-or-later; the full text is in COPYING next to this file.

What was copied: the 2D, single-workplane files of test/constraint/ (3D-only cases such as
pt_face_distance, pt_on_face, pt_plane_distance, pt_in_plane and free_in_3d* were left out),
plus the trivial `comment` case dropped as empty. The files are unmodified except that older
duplicates were removed: for most cases upstream keeps the same sketch saved by two older
file-format revisions (`*_v20.slvs`, `*_v22.slvs`); this corpus keeps the base file and the
`*_v22.slvs` re-save (labelled with the tag `format-v22`) as format-revision coverage and
drops the `*_v20.slvs` files.

Use: these files are read at test time by amg-sketch's corpus importer
(crates/amg-sketch/src/corpus/slvs.rs, written for Amalgam, not derived from SolveSpace
code). They are test data. They are never compiled into, linked with, or shipped in any
Amalgam binary or crate, and no SolveSpace source code is part of this repository.
Expectations (status, DOF) are in expected.json and were derived with Amalgam's own
reference oracle, not taken from SolveSpace.
